    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against right-handed starters. **Jackson Merrill** holds our highest daily efficiency score, buoyed by a prime #5 lineup spot and a high-probability environment for stolen bases against Pfaadt, where the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery (86th percentile) provides a crucial statistical edge for our SB-weighted strategy. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sees his score elevated by a strong platoon advantage against McGreevy, translating his #3 spot in the order into a high-ceiling output for R and RBI production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.07) remains a core start despite the slight drag from the dynamic platoon profile, as his raw power profile against Javier's high-xERA (5.27) matchup creates too much scoring potential to sit.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Cole Carrigg** (57.84), who narrowly missed the elite threshold but earned a start due to a significant 14% park factor boost. While **Cole Carrigg** remains a marginal play due to the lower-tier pitching skill of Seymour, his switch-hitting versatility and placement in the #3 spot keep him ahead of the remaining bench depth. We are forced to navigate this slate without **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jacob Wilson** due to scheduling, while **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, limiting our rotational flexibility. We will be monitoring **Nasim Nunez** (52.94) closely; his matchup against Nola presents the highest risk of the day, as Nola\u2019s elite ability to control the running game directly threatens our primary objective in the SB category. **Kyle Tucker** (65.22) and **Andy Pages** (61.68) provide solid stability, though their output against Boyd will be tempered by the left-on-left dynamic, requiring them to capitalize on park advantages to anchor the lineup.",
